WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.280
Guess who's back?

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:05.200
Well, you probably don’t need to be told,
since it's almost guaranteed that you and

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:09.250
everyone you know has been freaking out about
his return since the moment the Avengers:

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.240
Endgame trailer dropped.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.340
Yeah, you guessed it: it’s Hawkeye.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.900
“What, you didn’t see that coming?”

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.740
One person who has only just recently addressed
Clint Barton’s return to the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:23.010
Universe is the man behind the bow himself,
Jeremy Renner.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:26.920
Sure, the actor has been teasing fans for
months on end about his connection to the

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:32.220
fourth Avengers film, posting plenty of cheeky
snaps on Instagram with Avengers-related captions,

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:37.200
but Renner has mostly kept quiet about how
exactly Hawkeye will fit into the upcoming

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:37.860
movie’s story.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:42.160
That all changed when Marvel Studios rolled
out the trailer for Endgame, which revealed

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:46.480
Renner back in action not as Hawkeye, but
as Hawkeye's alter-ego Ronin.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:50.300
After the trailer debuted, Renner took to
Twitter to share the footage that Marvel had

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.260
released that morning, posting to his 4 million
followers:

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:54.540
"Good to see you all again!

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:55.520
Coming in hot!"

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:59.760
Renner then headed to his Instagram account
and uploaded the teaser poster for the film,

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:04.580
which confirmed the movie’s earlier-than-expected
release date of April 26th, 2019.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:05.800
Renner’s caption read:

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.100
"Anyone seen the trailer??"

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:11.030
Obviously, that’s kind of a silly question,
considering Endgame’s trailer set a new

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:16.760
record by racking up 289 million views in
the first 24 hours after its release.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:21.180
When Marvel fans first learned that Hawkeye
and Ant-Man wouldn't appear in Avengers: Infinity

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:26.280
War, the rumor mill began to crank out fan
theory after fan theory regarding their unknown

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:26.880
whereabouts.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.180
Infinity War did offer a brief explanation,
but it was pretty blink-and-you’ll-miss-it.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:32.020
“Where’s Clint?"

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:36.720
"After the whole Accord situation he and Scott
took a deal, it was too tough on their families

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:37.480
they're on house arrest.”

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:42.080
After Thanos loaded up the Infinity Gauntlet
with all six Infinity Stones, snapped his

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:47.120
fingers and wiped out half the universe in
the final moments of Infinity War, fans started

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.880
to freak, and who can blame them?

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:54.060
Audiences watched as beloved heroes like Scarlet
Witch, Star-Lord, Spider-Man, Black Panther

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:57.110
and many more faded into dusty nothingness.

00:01:57.110 --> 00:02:01.659
Worse still, Hawkeye and Ant-Man's fates were
left unclear since they weren't present on

00:02:01.659 --> 00:02:06.050
the battlefield, and so audiences were left
to wonder whether those two heroes had become

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:07.660
victims of the Decimation.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:12.280
Since Infinity War's ending, we've thankfully
learned that both Clint Barton and Scott Lang

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:13.060
are still alive.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:17.540
The end-credits scene of Ant-Man and the Wasp
confirmed Scott Lang’s survival, albeit

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:21.640
in a perilous state, stuck in the Quantum
Realm with no obvious means of escape.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:26.900
After a long wait, the Endgame trailer confirmed
that Hawkeye also survived the Decimation.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:31.740
But while Ant-Man seems in relative good spirits
in Endgame, Hawkeye is a different story.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:36.800
Suited up as Ronin, he looks as sleek as he
does intimidating, and it's evident that he's

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:41.120
gone through exactly the kind of trauma that
would push someone to transform into a rogue

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:41.700
assassin.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:46.280
Steve Rogers stating that the heroes lost
friends, family and a part of themselves following

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:51.340
Infinity War implies Hawkeye's family may
have disintegrated in the snap, spurring him

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:52.540
into becoming Ronin.

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:57.000
This is just a rumor for now, but Infinity
War and Endgame directors Joe and Anthony

00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:00.940
Russo had previously promised to cook up something
special for Hawkeye.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.180
“I knew I should have stretched.”

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:07.700
Throughout shooting on Endgame, Renner had
been generous with behind-the-scenes teases,

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:09.720
often uploading selfies taken on-set.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.800
In June, the actor teased on Instagram:

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:14.340
"Got this feelin I need to SUIT up soon."

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:18.620
Renner also turned things up a notch when
he uploaded a photo of himself from the last

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:19.860
day of filming on Endgame.

00:03:20.249 --> 00:03:24.120
And while his re-emergence in the franchise
was all but inevitable, it's nice to know

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:27.750
that Renner can now talk a little more openly
about Avengers: Endgame.

